    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">Hi Folks,<div><br></div><div>Sorry forgot to record/webcast the presentation on making a CV using RMarkdown. However, if you want to see the source material, it&#39;s on github here: </div><div><ul><li><a href=\"https://github.com/ryanpeek/markdown_cv\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://github.com/ryanpeek/markdown_cv&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792466910595000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1hX69qKo2d4PdfvMLDFwf8\">https://github.com/ryanpeek/markdown_cv</a><br></li></ul><div>I essentially took Steven Miller&#39;s excellent <a href=\"http://svmiller.com/blog/2016/03/svm-r-markdown-cv/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://svmiller.com/blog/2016/03/svm-r-markdown-cv/&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792466910595000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2PM_g3G-CaNcKFZ-pdXgdx\">post</a> and <a href=\"https://github.com/svmiller/svm-r-markdown-templates\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://github.com/svmiller/svm-r-markdown-templates&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792466910595000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0GCgBsNsNgpjh4wamfT-_P\">associated code</a> and utilized it with a few minor formatting changes. </div></div><div><br></div><div>Important tips:</div><div><ul><li>Use a new RStudio project for this (and everything, it makes things easier)</li><li>Make sure you have a LaTex distribution installed (<a href=\"http://www.latex-project.org/get/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://www.latex-project.org/get/&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792466910595000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0ukJajFVfo8rnHkqPogmec\">see here</a>, note: it is a big file and will take a little time to install the first time)</li><li>Make sure in your RStudio global settings you have <b>pdfLaTex</b> selected in the Sweave options (<a href=\"https://support.rstudio.com/hc/en-us/articles/200532257-Customizing-LaTeX-Options\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://support.rstudio.com/hc/en-us/articles/200532257-Customizing-LaTeX-Options&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792466910595000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1TN4mhP4MU7_za0b8MTM_i\">see here</a> for more info on checking this)</li><li>The RMarkdown (.Rmd) file (in my repo, I have a few versions) needs to be in the same place as the .tex file, which is the template that is used to render the document into a nice PDF. </li></ul></div></div><div class=\"gmail_extra\"><br><div class=\"gmail_quote\">On Wed, May 10, 2017 at 9:36 AM, Calvin Thigpen <span dir=\"ltr\">&lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">cgth...@ucdavis.edu</a>&gt;</span> wrote:<br><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0 0 0 .8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\">Hey Ryan,<div><br></div><div>I wasn&#39;t able to attend but am interested in reformatting my CV using RMarkdown. Do you have any code that you could share via GitHub?</div><div class=\"gmail_extra\"><br clear=\"all\"><div><div data-smartmail=\"gmail_signature\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div><div dir=\"ltr\"><div><div dir=\"ltr\"><div><div dir=\"ltr\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div style=\"font-size:small\">Thank you,</div><div style=\"font-size:small\"><br></div><div style=\"font-size:small\">Calvin Thigpen</div><div style=\"font-size:small\">PhD candidate</div><div style=\"font-size:small\"><span style=\"font-size:12.8px\">Transportation Technology &amp; Policy</span><br></div><div style=\"font-size:small\"><span style=\"font-size:12.8px\">University of California, Davis</span></div><div style=\"font-size:small\"><a href=\"http://www.calvinthigpen.com/\" style=\"color:rgb(17,85,204)\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://www.calvinthigpen.com/&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792466910595000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1mOdo0sIWLYHQTPjVII2Nn\">www.calvinthigpen.com</a></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div>\r\n<br><div class=\"gmail_quote\"></div></div></div></blockquote></div></div>"
    ],
